            "created_at": "2025-07-12T07:00:59.675677+00:00",
            "notes": "# -----------------------------------\n\n# **Items**\n\n###  [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) \n\n###  [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) \n\nSell greens as needed.\n\n [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) is a great early game item in general, especially on Soldier, since he doesn't *need* a huge gun buff early on and it's a really cheap way to get 10% AP. Technically  [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) is an even cheaper way but we already have that.\n\n [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) might just be the best blue item in the game (not considering hero items, that's probably orisa's  [Enhanced Target Sensors](item_d2e9e06c-5315-4ddb-b86a-d0397bd4dbbd) seriously that item is broken) because its CDR is half of  [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e)'s CDR but like only 35% of the cost. That's, like, 15% better. Also more AP for rockets.\n\nIf your team comp is more brawl-y then I like  [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0), it's not nearly as good as the other two items but if you're rich and want to brawl a little more or you are just standing closer to the enemy this will provide some help with brawling for longer",
